      "message": "So on \"\\r\" (two empty lines) the loop above kicks out one empty line and then this used to kick out the last empty line but now does not. Interestingly on \"\" this used to kick out the one (empty) line. However, something like \"foo\\r\" used to get \"foo\" on a line, the `\\r` is skipped, then this kicked out the trailing empty line.\n\nI don\u0027t see how the old code is incorrect unless `\\r` really wants to mean \"line end\" and not \"line break\". But this is essentially the same as seeing if the last character of the overall string is `\\r` and just ignoring it if it is? Seems like that would be easier to reason about and makes it more obvious what the oddity is?",
